{
  "question_id": "q_068_sales_team_compensation",
  "slug": "sales-team-compensation",
  "title": "Sales Team Compensation",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "company": "Oracle",
  "premium": true,
  "question": "Oracle enterprise sales operations calculates annual compensation from each rep's contract.\n\nEvery rep earns their `base` salary. On deal volume **up to their quota** they earn the `commission` rate (for example `0.1` is 10%). Any deal volume **above the quota** earns an accelerated rate of `commission * accelerator` (for example `0.1 * 1.5 = 15%`).\n\n`total_compensation = base + commission * min(total_deals, quota) + commission * accelerator * max(total_deals - quota, 0)`\n\nReps with no deals have a total deal volume of 0. Write a query to calculate each rep's total compensation, rounded to 2 decimal places. Output `employee_id` and `total_compensation`, sorted by `employee_id` in ascending order.",
  "notes": [
    "Employee 101 closed 800,000 against a 500,000 quota: 60,000 base + 10% of 500,000 + 15% of the 300,000 above quota = 155,000.",
    "Employee 102 stayed under quota: 50,000 base + 10% of 300,000 = 80,000."
  ],
  "tables": [
    {
      "table_name": "employee_contract",
      "columns": [
        {
          "column_name": "employee_id",
          "data_type": "INT"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "base",
          "data_type": "INT"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "commission",
          "data_type": "DOUBLE"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "quota",
          "data_type": "INT"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "accelerator",
          "data_type": "DOUBLE"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "table_name": "deals",
      "columns": [
        {
          "column_name": "employee_id",
          "data_type": "INT"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "deal_size",
          "data_type": "INT"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sample_data": {
    "employee_contract": [
      {
        "employee_id": 101,
        "base": 60000,
        "commission": 0.1,
        "quota": 500000,
        "accelerator": 1.5
      },
      {
        "employee_id": 102,
        "base": 50000,
        "commission": 0.1,
        "quota": 400000,
        "accelerator": 1.5
      }
    ],
    "deals": [
      {
        "employee_id": 101,
        "deal_size": 400000
      },
      {
        "employee_id": 101,
        "deal_size": 400000
      },
      {
        "employee_id": 102,
        "deal_size": 100000
      },
      {
        "employee_id": 102,
        "deal_size": 200000
      }
    ]
  },
  "sample_output": [
    {
      "employee_id": 101,
      "total_compensation": 155000
    },
    {
      "employee_id": 102,
      "total_compensation": 80000
    }
  ],
  "reference_sql": "WITH deal_totals AS (\n  SELECT employee_id, SUM(deal_size) AS total_deals\n  FROM deals\n  GROUP BY employee_id\n)\nSELECT\n  c.employee_id,\n  ROUND(c.base\n        + c.commission * LEAST(IFNULL(d.total_deals, 0), c.quota)\n        + c.commission * c.accelerator * GREATEST(IFNULL(d.total_deals, 0) - c.quota, 0), 2) AS total_compensation\nFROM employee_contract c\nLEFT JOIN deal_totals d ON c.employee_id = d.employee_id\nORDER BY c.employee_id;",
